exports[`native BPMN interaction contract parsing > rejects dynamic question refs that would otherwise leak raw JSON into pi-ask 1`] = `
"[pi-wendao.runtime.invalid_dynamic_question] Error: Invalid dynamic question payload

Consumer activity: Task_DynamicChoiceInput
Variable: currentQuestion
Problem: ref did not resolve to a non-empty string
Bad payload: {"prompt":"Which repair path should the workflow use?","choices":["minimal","broaden"]}

Help: currentQuestion must be a non-empty string used as the user-facing prompt.
Contract: bpmn.native_human_task_io.v1 requires question source values to be prompt text, not JSON objects.

Expected value:
\`\`\`json
{
  "currentQuestion": "Which repair path should the workflow use?"
}
\`\`\`"
`;

exports[`native BPMN interaction contract parsing > rejects producer choice_array outputs whose items are strings 1`] = `
"[pi-wendao.runtime.invalid_dynamic_choices] Error: Invalid dynamic choices payload

Producer activity: Task_PrepareQuestion
Variable: currentChoices
Item: 1
Problem: item is not an object
Bad payload: "Graph visualization (workflow display and node rendering)"

Help: currentChoices must be a native Array<{ value: string; label?: string; description?: string }>; do not wrap the array in a JSON string.
Contract: native choices data must be a JSON array whose items have a non-empty string value.

Expected value:
\`\`\`json
{
  "currentChoices": [
    {
      "value": "minimal",
      "label": "Minimal repair",
      "description": "Repair only the failing contract."
    }
  ]
}
\`\`\`"
`;
